"notes": [
"Game Changers list is 53 cards as of 2026-10-10 (Scryfall is:gamechanger).",
"Feb 9, 2026: Farewell and Biorhythm added to Game Changers; Biorhythm unbanned straight onto the list (Wizards).",
"Feb 9, 2026: Lutri, the Spellchaser unbanned, but still banned as a companion (Wizards, secondary detail).",
"Feb 9, 2026: no bracket rule changes; panel said none until after a MagicCon; brackets still labelled beta.",
"Oct 21, 2025: tutor limits removed from all brackets; the best tutors are policed by the Game Changers list instead.",
"Oct 21, 2025: ten cards left Game Changers: Expropriate; Jin-Gitaxias, Core Augur; Sway of the Stars; Vorinclex, Voice of Hunger; Kinnan, Bonder Prodigy; Urza, Lord High Artificer; Winota, Joiner of Forces; Yuriko, the Tiger's Shadow; Deflecting Swat; Food Chain.",
"Oct 21, 2025: each bracket now has a minimum game length (9/8/6/4 turns, any in cEDH); Bracket 2 no longer means 'a precon'.",
"Bracket rules still in force: no mass land denial in Brackets 1-3; no intentional two-card infinite combos in 1-2; no extra-turn cards in 1; extra turns not chained in 2-3.",
"Banned list (83 cards) still includes the Sept 2024 bans: Dockside Extortionist; Jeweled Lotus; Mana Crypt; Nadu, Winged Wisdom.",
"March, May and June 2026 ban announcements had no Commander changes (secondary sources). Nothing found for July-October 2026.",
"Aug 7, 2026 rules change: abilities that add mana and also move a card to or from the library are no longer mana abilities (about ten cards, e.g. Odyssey Eggs).",
"Staples are ranked by EDHREC inclusion over the past 2 years; edhrecPct = share of eligible decks that play the card.",
"Dual and tri lands sit in 'multi'; colourless-identity lands (Command Tower, fetches, utility lands) sit in 'colorless'."
]
